WEBVTT

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:09.970
Come on, Tokimune.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.470
Get up already.

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:17.220
So,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.210
where were you planning on taking that machine?

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:23.320
To my company's service center in Arandas.

00:00:25.930 --> 00:00:27.920
I'm Jamie Hazaford,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.240
Kivernas Manufacturing Company engineer.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.130
Kivernas? Do you recall any
manufacturers with that name?

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.920
We're an up-and-coming company!

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:43.240
We're rising fast in the industry
with our revolutionary Arge-vo-vollen!

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:47.580
That machine is called Arge-vollen?

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.010
Yes!

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.380
Argevollen S-Stablis Prima.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:52.760
It utilizes the latest... U-Link system...

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.050
to copy a dedicated
operator's thought patterns

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.890
into a Trail Krieger's control system...

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:00.890
to radically...

00:01:00.890 --> 00:01:01.850
improve its capabilities.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.290
It's a groundbreaking endeavor!

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.030
By using this system, Argevo-ve-vollen—

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:09.400
We're leaving.

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.780
We'll get as far away from here as we can before dark.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.330
Bring the girl with us.

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:19.290
Yes, sir.

00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:27.610
Tokimune, get moving!

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:28.800
Okay!

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:34.950
Someday, in this space deprived of hope,
kono takaki mubou no kuu de itsuka

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:39.620
you'll kneel of your own will.
sono ishi wa hiza wo tateru

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:49.920
break up foreordination

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:50.810
Silver Will
break up foreordination

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:50.870
break up foreordination

00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:55.740
Was that flame an illusion or a friend?
fake ano hi wa nakama ka

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:00.470
Am I to venture into the darkness?
susumu beki wa yami ka

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:01.060
No place

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:09.790
You'll find nameless emotions beyond the protruding knife.
knife tsukitateta saki ni shoutai no mienu kanjou

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.570
I can't let this end here yet.
ima wa mada koko de owarenai

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:20.740
I need to get ready to survive.
naraba ikiru junbi wo shiro yo

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.010
The passion in my heart only burns hotter.
uzu takaku tsumiageteku netsujou

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:29.550
Needless to say, it burdens me.
omotai ni kimatten darou

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:31.000
wake up your tough intention

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:31.950
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
wake up your tough intention

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:36.190
mijuku da to warau ga ii sa senjou
Go ahead and mock my inexperience on the battlefield.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:42.830
I'll show you what I've got, bit by bit,
hitotsu zutsu tashikamete yaru kara

00:02:43.270 --> 00:02:44.420
so bring it on.
kakattekoi

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:54.860
break up foreordination

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:10.880
Awakening

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:20.330
Tokimune, walk properly!

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.840
Whose fault do you think it is
that we had to change our route?

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.530
It's my fault! And I'm trying!

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.100
I'm trying...

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.340
I'm sorry. I don't feel so good.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.810
Deal with it. Just swallow it
until we get to the next point.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.640
They get along so well.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.600
We're heading directly into the middle
of the enemy we were trying to avoid.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.050
That's true.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.340
Are you okay?

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.240
I-I'm okay!

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.790
I'm relieved.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:04.040
I can see that, if nothing else,
you're not a soldier.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.280
It looks like they were
transporting a Trail Krieger.

00:04:16.280 --> 00:04:19.530
And someone tried to get it for
themselves and got wiped out?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:20.920
Probably.

00:04:21.710 --> 00:04:23.240
Contact the Colonel immediately.

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:24.080
Yes, sir.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:29.190
We'll try a different pattern
for the boot-up process.

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:33.060
I know. We'll clear the memory
banks while loading the ID code,

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:35.360
and then do an emergency
start-up of the generator.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.400
Okay, can I do this?

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.710
Connecting generator to drive.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:48.110
Stabilizing gyros. I'll keep one leg
fixed and move the other forward.

00:04:56.630 --> 00:04:59.540
That's enough, Silfy. Come on out.

00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.500
It's been like this since we
pulled Tokimune out of it.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.100
It won't even budge.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:09.310
We tried every pattern we could
think of, but nothing worked.

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:13.320
I've never seen a machine that didn't
work like everything else in a war.

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:15.590
I told you, the U-Link system

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:19.080
records the thought patterns of the first person to pilot it.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.040
He's basically the start-up key now!

00:05:22.040 --> 00:05:23.950
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:26.580
Sorry. Soldiers only trust in their own experience.

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:29.520
How's the pilot, Private Susumu?

00:05:29.520 --> 00:05:33.080
Ah, well... It was his first fight, you know.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.860
I suppose so, it's only to be expected on his first time.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.500
What should we do, Captain?

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.340
Didn't the girl just tell us?

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:47.140
We let Private Susumu pilot it.

00:05:48.420 --> 00:05:50.460
The enemy will be here soon.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:53.840
Now that he's the key,
let him do his job as such.

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.610
This is war.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.620
These are all the soldiers who surrendered.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.120
For now.

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.940
I'm sure there'll be more.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.740
Our forces will counterattack!

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:18.200
Okay, take them.

00:06:18.200 --> 00:06:19.350
This way.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.090
How far along are the preparations?

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.150
We're running a cleanup operation,

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:28.470
which means our forces at
the rear are running behind.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.990
But I believe we'll make it
in time for the operation.

00:06:30.990 --> 00:06:31.850
Make sure we do.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:35.600
The final target of the invasion
is the enemy capital.

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.880
If we can't make good use of our
Trail Kriegers, the operation has no point.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:41.190
Yes, sir.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.360
So,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.200
let's hear your report
about this mystery battle.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:01.760
A battering?

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.250
You mean it was a melee battle?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:06.420
Yes. They say it was fought
with neither gun nor sword.

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:11.690
I didn't think Arandas had any
Trail Krieger that could do that.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:15.900
It doesn't. To be honest,
they're all far outdated.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:17.020
A new type?

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:21.640
Everything at the scene, except for one
Arandas mech, was of our own forces.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.280
But they had no known affiliation.
It was likely camouflage.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.130
We can't confirm who any of
the soldiers belong to, either.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:30.540
Enemy camouflage? Or...

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:33.330
What shall we do?

00:07:33.330 --> 00:07:36.520
I want to know where this
new Trail Krieger went.

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.320
Keep pursuing and investigating it.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.790
Intelligence may be involved.

00:07:41.790 --> 00:07:44.300
I'll figure out something to tell the brass.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:47.840
I'll send a message to the forces
still fighting the survivors.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.180
Thanks.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:04.500
Okay!

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.190
Listen up.

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:06.820
Postural control is your first priority.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.210
Your center of gravity isn't your heel!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:10.620
Go forward!

00:08:10.620 --> 00:08:11.820
Forward...

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:27.590
What was that? That was
worse than last time!

00:08:27.590 --> 00:08:29.880
This is what happens when
I do what you tell me to!

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:33.300
Why was it so easy back then?

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.510
If only I knew that...

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:35.970
Give me a second!

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:39.670
Besides, you're just reading
out of that guide!

00:08:39.670 --> 00:08:40.860
Are you really an engineer?

00:08:40.860 --> 00:08:42.030
How rude!

00:08:42.030 --> 00:08:44.080
I'm integral to Argevollen's—

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.800
Then why won't it work?

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:47.400
Isn't it supposed to be a
groundbreaking system?

00:08:48.950 --> 00:08:50.160
Well...

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.950
That was my first fight.

00:08:53.950 --> 00:08:56.560
I was so focused on the task,
I don't remember anything.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.810
But next time...

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:02.040
Hey, what am I doing wrong?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.800
Help me out here!

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.480
There was a refinery here,

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:26.730
so there's a large flue built into this
mountain, separate from the mines.

00:09:26.730 --> 00:09:28.620
We'll have to go through here.

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.100
Seeker, go on ahead.

00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:30.780
Roger.

00:09:37.510 --> 00:09:38.880
We'll be done soon.

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:41.460
I see. The enemy's very brave.

00:09:41.460 --> 00:09:42.440
That's true.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.790
But the real problem is the
ones who just keep running.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:48.780
Problem? Aren't they just cowards?

00:09:48.780 --> 00:09:53.300
There are those in the fleeing army
who understand the point of running away.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:57.420
Our job is to nip those future
powerful enemies in the bud.

00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.610
Remember that.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:00.010
Right.

00:10:00.010 --> 00:10:01.680
An old abandoned mine...

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:03.270
What's going on here?

00:10:03.270 --> 00:10:04.940
Garm 1 is en route.

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:29.630
You can finally keep rations down now, huh?

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:31.630
How are you feeling?

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:33.740
So-so. I'll do my best.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.200
You're working hard.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.890
Everyone recognizes that.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:43.120
Silfy says you've got a long way to go,

00:10:43.960 --> 00:10:46.640
but you're the only one
who can pilot Argevollen.

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:47.770
Do your best.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:49.920
We're leaving.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:51.030
Yes Ma'am!

00:10:55.720 --> 00:10:58.280
Remember! Remember, Jamie!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.260
You learned this!

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:03.410
Remember!

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:18.930
So there are caves like these down here?

00:11:18.930 --> 00:11:20.800
It's not a cave, it's a flue.

00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:21.530
They Flew?

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:22.400
Who?

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:23.930
It's a path for smoke to escape.

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.280
Now shut up and walk.

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:25.940
Yessir.

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:27.380
Good grief...

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.440
Hey, noobie, hurry up!

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.680
Yessir!

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:06.190
You don't control it.

00:12:06.190 --> 00:12:07.690
What do you do?

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:12.690
I'm so stupid!

00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.730
S-Sorry, I was talking to myself.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.620
I knew they'd be here.

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:32.670
They got rid of their trucks?

00:12:32.670 --> 00:12:33.880
Which means...

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:35.320
What do you see, G2?

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:36.170
Nothing.

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:37.720
I'm heading to the mountain.

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:39.010
Stay sharp.

00:12:39.010 --> 00:12:40.150
I know.

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:58.320
All right. Continue observation.

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:03.990
Captain Samonji.

00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:06.200
They're here. Three units.

00:13:06.200 --> 00:13:07.910
I see. Tanita?

00:13:07.910 --> 00:13:09.000
All ready.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:09.740
We're leaving.

00:13:09.740 --> 00:13:10.390
Hurry!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.000
Right!

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:14.490
Tokimune's unit is falling behind.

00:13:14.490 --> 00:13:15.500
What will we do?

00:13:31.130 --> 00:13:33.330
We can't cross the mountain like this.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:34.270
Come back, G2.

00:13:34.270 --> 00:13:36.200
We've found what appears to be their escape path.

00:13:36.200 --> 00:13:37.440
Roger.

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.290
Can you hear me, Private Susumu?

00:13:55.290 --> 00:13:56.170
Y-Yes.

00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:59.170
The enemy is following us down this flue.

00:14:00.630 --> 00:14:02.680
Hey, what are we going to do?

00:14:02.680 --> 00:14:03.950
Shut up!

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.000
No, nothing!

00:14:09.460 --> 00:14:13.160
This wasn't the plan,
but you're now the rear guard.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:16.420
You learned what that means in school, right?

00:14:16.420 --> 00:14:17.790
Yes...

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.550
It's the rear guard's duty

00:14:19.550 --> 00:14:23.950
to halt the enemy's advance and allow the allies time to escape.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:27.200
This is an order.

00:14:27.200 --> 00:14:28.810
Stop them!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:32.850
I repeat:

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:35.580
Hold the enemy there.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:39.740
Private Okui will take Jamie-san
and catch up to the rest of us.

00:14:39.740 --> 00:14:40.590
Roger.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:42.120
Wait a second!

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.960
What about Argevollen?
What about that guy Tokimune?

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:48.020
We'll engage the enemy to cover you.

00:14:48.020 --> 00:14:50.280
It's dangerous, so get out of there—

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.100
You're sacrificing him?

00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:55.000
You confiscated Argevollen and now you're going to abandon it?

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.220
That's terrible! It's so selfish!

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:59.980
Only Private Susumu can use Argevollen.

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:03.010
The survival of the squad is at stake here.

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:04.140
Please understand.

00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.400
That's...

00:15:05.400 --> 00:15:07.350
I thought you were a good person!

00:15:07.350 --> 00:15:07.820
How can you say that?

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:08.870
It's all right.
How can you say that?

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:11.800
You're leaving a raw recruit
behind while you run away?

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:12.150
That's horrible!

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:13.450
It's fine!
That's horrible!

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.360
I'm a soldier.

00:15:17.010 --> 00:15:19.390
Soldiers must obey orders.

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:21.760
Civilians should stay out of it.

00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:24.280
But no matter how you look at it, that order's ridiculous!

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:28.330
You disobeyed orders to save me, didn't you?

00:15:28.330 --> 00:15:30.320
This is the best choice right now.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.350
That's right.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:32.950
Okui, hurry.

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:33.440
Right!

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.350
W-Wait!

00:15:37.850 --> 00:15:39.130
I'm sorry.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:31.740
Oh yeah!

00:16:33.230 --> 00:16:34.230
Hey!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.160
Hey, wait!

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:51.680
What do I do?

00:17:04.940 --> 00:17:06.480
What should I do?

00:17:19.320 --> 00:17:20.210
Mental image!

00:17:23.860 --> 00:17:27.010
I'm sorry... I didn't say it right!

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:30.050
Don't think about
controlling it properly.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:34.050
Imagine what you want to do!

00:17:34.050 --> 00:17:36.810
Not victory, or acknowledgement!

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.600
Think of survival!

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:40.810
Hey, you!

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:42.560
Wait!

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.850
Just stay put!

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.320
Don't run off on your own!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.070
Put me down! I'm going to
stay with Argevollen—

00:17:49.070 --> 00:17:51.820
I've been ordered to bring you back safely!

00:17:51.820 --> 00:17:53.560
Forget that!

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.340
Move.

00:18:14.350 --> 00:18:15.720
No, that's not it...

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:41.490
G2!

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:54.470
What the hell is that?

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:57.180
Is that the new type the captain was talking about?

00:18:59.100 --> 00:19:00.180
That's right.

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:03.630
The manual I learned in training doesn't matter.

00:19:03.630 --> 00:19:05.190
Punch, kick...!

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:08.080
There's only one of them!
We'll hit from both sides! Help me!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:08.940
Roger!

00:19:10.200 --> 00:19:11.690
If I don't fight, they'll kill me!

00:19:11.690 --> 00:19:13.770
I can't die here!

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.720
Are you okay, G3?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:19.660
I can still move!

00:19:34.340 --> 00:19:37.220
Damn it! What is this thing?

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:49.720
I'm screwed. What do I do?

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:51.480
Come here, Tokimune!

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:55.750
Follow him!

00:19:55.750 --> 00:19:56.320
Right!

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:22.760
Duck!

00:20:31.460 --> 00:20:34.110
You're as good as ever.

00:20:34.110 --> 00:20:35.530
I'm in love.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:37.320
Same goes for you, pretty boy.

00:20:55.240 --> 00:20:58.440
That will keep them off our back for a while.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:02.430
We don't know how many
more are out there, though.

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:08.030
Suzushiro, what do you think about that lady?

00:21:08.030 --> 00:21:09.720
You mean Jamie-san?

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:12.440
They pair well, her and Tokimune-kun.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:14.840
I see.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.580
Hazaford-san.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:20.930
Call me Jamie.

00:21:20.930 --> 00:21:23.720
Oh... Jamie, then...

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:27.200
Thanks... you saved me.

00:21:27.810 --> 00:21:29.350
Likewise.

00:21:29.350 --> 00:21:31.210
You and I are even now.

00:21:40.370 --> 00:21:42.720
What do you intend to do with that?

00:21:48.380 --> 00:21:51.070
Ah, pardon me...

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.230
We're leaving.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:55.980
Yes, sir.

00:23:36.370 --> 00:23:37.520
One Man Army

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:39.330
"One Man Army."
One Man Army

00:23:39.330 --> 00:23:39.340
One Man Army
